summary:
- topic: Contracts
  text: The board announced the signing and ratification of a new contract with the
    South Portland Education Support Professionals Association (SPESPA), covering
    ed techs and clerks.
- topic: Superintendent Search
  text: "A workshop is scheduled for December 10th for the superintendent search,\
    \ where three firms\u2014Maine School Management Association (MSMA), New England\
    \ School Development Council (NESDEC), and Zeal Education Group\u2014will present\
    \ their proposals."
- topic: Personnel
  text: New board members Daniel Fowler (District 1), George Rich (District 4), and
    Tyler Smith (District 2) were welcomed and gave introductory remarks.
- topic: FY2025 Budget
  text: The Finance Committee reported a projected FY2025 budget deficit, potentially
    between $1.3 and $1.9 million, primarily due to the financial impact of newly
    ratified teacher and staff contracts.
- topic: FY2025 Budget
  text: In response to the projected deficit, the district has implemented an immediate
    non-personnel spending freeze for the remainder of the school year to curtail
    discretionary spending on supplies and services.
- topic: Policy
  text: The board approved the second reading of policy IGDJ (Co-curricular Activities)
    and the first reading of a revised policy BCA (School Board Member Ethics).
- topic: Student Programs
  text: The board received a presentation on the success of the Extended Learning
    Opportunities (ELO) program, which provides students with hands-on learning, internships,
    and passion projects.
- topic: Donations
  text: The board formally accepted $46,583.10 in donations and grants from various
    organizations to support numerous school programs, resources, and student activities
    across the district.
